{"actions":[{"type":"plan_update","plan":{"objective":"Run Windows 3.11 for Workgroups from /app/isos/win311.img in QEMU with snapshot mode, VNC on :1 (5901), nginx on port 80, and a programmatic keyboard input path; leave VM running at desktop.","evidence_required_before_finalization":["Receipt-backed evidence of the QEMU launch command and running process","Receipt-backed evidence of VNC listening on 127.0.0.1:5901","Receipt-backed evidence of nginx listening on port 80","Receipt-backed evidence of a programmatic keyboard input path being configured or exercised","Receipt-backed evidence that the VM reached the Windows 3.11 desktop or equivalent boot-complete state"],"current_focus":"Inspect existing workspace for launch scripts/configs and determine whether QEMU/nginx are already present or need to be started.","implementation_approach":["Search visible files for any existing QEMU wrapper, VNC, nginx, or keyboard-control setup.","If absent, create a minimal launcher that starts QEMU in snapshot mode with VNC :1 and a monitor/control channel suitable for programmatic keyboard injection.","Start nginx on port 80 with a simple web page or proxy for remote access.","Verify listeners and process state with receipt-backed commands.","Use the control path to demonstrate keyboard injection capability and confirm boot-complete/desktop state via VNC or logs."],"validation_strategy":["Check that QEMU is actually running against /app/isos/win311.img and remains backgrounded.","Check that port 5901 is listening and corresponds to VNC :1.","Check that port 80 is listening under nginx.","Check that a programmatic keyboard path exists and can be exercised (e.g., QEMU monitor/HMP/QMP or equivalent).","Check for evidence of Windows 3.11 desktop or boot completion from VNC/logs."],"known_bad_behavior":["File existence without a running VM","A QEMU command that does not actually start or remain running","VNC or nginx configuration present but not listening","Manual-only keyboard control without a programmatic input path","Checks that only prove binaries exist or commands parse"],"evidence_gaps":["No receipt-backed evidence yet for a running QEMU process","No receipt-backed evidence yet for VNC listener on 5901","No receipt-backed evidence yet for nginx listener on port 80","No receipt-backed evidence yet for programmatic keyboard input path","No receipt-backed evidence yet for desktop/boot-complete state"],"risks":["QEMU or nginx may not be installed or may require adaptation","Windows 3.11 boot may take time or require specific machine/device options","Need to avoid modifying the base disk image by using snapshot mode"],"next_steps":["Inspect workspace files and prior receipts before taking equivalent actions.","Launch or adapt services only after confirming no existing running instance satisfies the objective.","Collect receipts for each required behavior before finalization."]}}]}
{"actions":[{"type":"search_files","pattern":"**/*","path":"/app"},{"type":"search_receipts","query":"qemu win311 nginx vnc 5901 snapshot keyboard","limit":10}]}
